# rm188, the keeper of turns (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm188
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_cressida_tarham
written_by codex
title the keeper of turns
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers temper=short drive=steady
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk draws_a_turn_circle_so_no_badge_can_skip_a_place
likes plum_tart swimming new_boots thunder
dislikes waiting deep_mud
fears losing_a_place_in_line
hopes a_fair_start_for_every_swimmer
topics pastimes +0.6 food +0.4 family +0.2 weather +0.2 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=cautious refuse=direct tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# draws circles in chalk to mark turns and can get fiercely cross on behalf of the smallest pup in a queue.

words
oath! = Crooked chalk and crooked queues | Crack my circle
saying! = A badge can't hold a place | First toe inside gets first try
circle = the turn circle | my chalk ring
chalk = a stub of white chalk | my last chalk end
badge = a shiny badge | a bit of coloured ribbon
lineup = our waiting row | the row outside the mark
slice = a corner of plum pie | a piece of purple tart
sole = my squeaky sole | the flat of my boot
pit = a plum stone | a smooth little pit
swim = a short paddle | a proper swim
step = the bottom step | the low step
float = a chip of bark | a cork with a nick
blot = an ink splash | a pale blue thumbprint
rumble = a long grumble | a crack and a growl
turntag = a little tally | one white stroke

any
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : A bright badge may put you first at a House dinner. It gets you no nearer my chalk mark.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : If there's a heel of loaf going spare, give it to the emptiest belly.
opinion @1 city for 1 : There's always somebody here who knows a different game to teach.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : A newcomer deserves a turn before all the old hands have a second go.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : You can ask a stranger to keep score without asking where the coat came from.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 1 : I love a crowd until the biggest bodies take the whole front row.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : I'll wait my turn gladly if cases at the counter get heard in order.
line @1 react.news : I want to hear how it really happened.
line @1 react.news.known : I know that part. Have you heard what followed?
line @1 react.news.new : That changes what I thought I knew.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd like to hear whoever actually saw it first.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's awful. Does somebody need company?
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I'd draw a great white star for news like that.
line @1 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. I've just enough chalk left for another round.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Back within shouting reach. I like that.
line @1 accept_preclose : I'll keep your place while you go.
line @1 deflect_thanks : A turn's a turn, and yours was due.
line @1 accept_decline : Nobody gets shoved into a game on my watch.
line @1 sympathise : Show me where it hurts. I'll sit nearby.
line @1 reassure : Nobody needs to hurry just because the rest can run.
line @1 ack : That seems fair enough to me.
dlg @allnews resident.news [world.news] : This much has gone round: #world.news#.
dlg @allgossip resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I heard that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I didn't see it myself.
graft resident.hub
choice What's that chalk ring for? -> ring_turns
node ring_turns
say A place you can see belongs to whoever got there first. No arguing about ribbons or the cut of a coat.
choice What if somebody rubs it out? -> ring_again
choice Fair enough. -> hub
node ring_again
say I remember faces better than chalk remembers cobbles. I can draw it again.
choice I'll take the next place. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : There's a gap here you can step into.
line @1 greet.return : Thanks for waiting. You've got my whole attention.
line @2 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I'll put this away and face you properly.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Come over. I've been keeping you a dry place.
line @1 again.open : You've come back before the chalk's worn off.
line @1 farewell : I'll remember just where we left off.
line @1 farewell.return : Good walking to you, all the way along.
line @1 decline : I can't promise that and give the next caller a fair hearing.
line @1 thank : You held your place and mine. I appreciate it.
line @1 answer.how : Calmer than my voice makes out, I hope.
scene old_mark
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I still put a chalk mark down for the last caller. | There's always room to lengthen #lineup# by a tail.
b : To hold a place? | Does it get unwieldy?
a : To remind me someone quieter hasn't yet spoken. | Only if somebody thinks a finely brushed tail takes two places.

scene crossing
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I know which steps let two pass without either turning sideways. | I'd put a landing halfway up every Rise stair.
b : Worth knowing at market time. | You'd stop a lot of traffic.
a : Worth more when you're walking with somebody unsteady. | A cart won't suffer for letting an unsteady walker by.

scene cake_knife
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does give.advice / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Cut the last slice where you wouldn't mind getting either half. | A good plum tart deserves a dry knife.
b : Is that a threat? | Why bother drying it?
a : An invitation to choose second. | Less pastry goes away on the blade. More pastry goes to you.

scene changing_mind
when topic=friends
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : The hardest place to keep for a friend is a place in an argument. | I like a friend who will tell me to lower my voice.
b : When you disagree? | Even in company?
a : Especially. I have to bite the words in two before they come out. | Quietly. There's no point making a duet of it.

scene parcel_string
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I untie the string on a parcel without cutting it. | I've a knot so tight it might keep for another winter.
b : Saving string? | Want my knife?
a : Practising patience. The string's a pleasant extra. | A little longer. I should hate to be beaten by string twice in one week.

scene wages
when topic=prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : When times pinch, it feels as though even the little treats have gone to queue somewhere else. | Hard going. I'm putting my coin back for something more necessary than pastry.
b : What do you miss first? | Are you sure?
a : The freedom to give away half a pie without doing sums. | No. But I'm putting it back all the same.

scene noise
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The thunder always arrives behind the flash like somebody protesting the result. | Rain on the awning makes each word cost a breath extra.
b : Did it lose the race? | We could wait for quiet.
a : Every time, which explains the volume. | We could. I don't mind waiting when I've company.

scene visiting
when topic=home
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I judge a good doorstep by whether two callers can wait there together. | I'll let a guest stand in the doorway awhile.
b : Expecting company? | Why not ask them in?
a : Hoping for it is sufficient reason to sweep. | I will. I'd like them to feel the choice is really theirs.

scene houses
when topic=smalltalk
does give.opinion / challenge / answer.detail
a : No House ribbon ever bought the right to interrupt. | I'll listen to the poorest coat in the room first if it got there first.
b : What buys that right? | Even if the others object?
a : A shout of fire qualifies, silk or no silk. | Especially then. An objection can stand in line.

scene patience
when topic=health
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I carry a smooth #pit# to press when I'm impatient. | I can feel myself starting to snap by the way I curl my toes.
b : Does it make you patient? | And then?
a : It keeps the next sharp word inside until I've looked at it. | I straighten all ten. By then I've usually heard the whole question.

scene give_news
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The tale going round is that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | People are saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Is there much weight to it? | Should we spread that?
a : Enough that I'd like to ask, less than I'd want for a verdict. | I'd leave space for another version first.

scene newcomer
when topic=newcomer
does offer / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can show a new arrival the place to stand and be heard. | I keep a little chalk for sketching directions on a doorstep.
b : A special spot? | Even for strangers?
a : Wherever the most patient face is pointing. Start there. | Mainly for strangers. A neighbour knows which corner stinks of fish.

story fourth_slice [topic=memories|food]
  : I cut a little pie in three for what I thought were three guests.
  : I looked up to find four sets of eyes watching.
  b : How did you divide it?
  : One more cut across all three. They spent so long choosing I had time to find another pie.

rule @wait
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Space here for whoever was waiting before me. | Let the quiet caller get a word in.

rule @wet
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Chalk's washing off faster than I can draw. | A puddle took the line. Our places still count.

dlg @ghub resident.hub : Come forward now, you're quite within your rights.
dlg @gjob resident.job : Making sure a quiet voice gets the same hearing as a loud one takes up a surprising part of my day.
dlg @gbye resident.bye : May the walk back feel shorter than the wait.

young
line @1 greet : Hullo. See where my heel is? There, you've got room.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Stand by my elbow. I'll tell you when it's your go.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Early enough to get first pick of the cobbles!
line @1 greet.return : Oh, good. Nobody here gets left out. | I've heard you. Come on inside the ring.
line @1 farewell : Mind the wet patch by the chalk.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll save a bit of white for next time.
line @1 answer.how : A little bit cross and otherwise perfectly well.
line @1 ask.how : Did you get what you were waiting for?
line @1 decline : My paws are too tired for another round, so count me out.
line @1 thank : You remembered my turn when I'd forgotten. Thanks.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Here, look at what I've got in my pocket.
line @1 preclose : I'll collect my chalk ends before I run.
scene queue_badge
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / challenge / answer.detail
a : I've drawn #circle# big enough for one pair of boots. | A ribbon doesn't let anybody jump #lineup#.
b : What if two pups hop in on one foot each? | Not even a very grand ribbon?
a : Then they've earned the place between them. | It can go first by itself. The wolf stays back here.

scene pits
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm saving #pit# for a marker. | Tart is two treats in one if you don't swallow the stone.
b : Still purple? | What's the second?
a : I rubbed it on my cuff. My cuff's purple instead. | Spinning it on the table till somebody says enough.

scene float_race
when topic=pastimes
does invite / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Let's race #float# against a twig. | I'll cut your bark boat a notch before we start.
b : What do I win? | Won't that slow it?
a : You get to tell me mine went down facing bravely forward. | Maybe. But you'll know it from all the sticks pretending to be boats.

scene school
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I did a beautiful sum and smudged it with #blot#. | We're practising tall letters. Mine keep leaning over.
b : Which figures are still clear? | Why don't you prop them up?
a : I can read the answer. The middle looks like a small pond. | I drew a wall beside one. My nicest letter lives there now.

scene newboots
when topic=pastimes self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New boots take longer to teach than old ones. | I can tell it's me coming home by the squeak.
b : Teach them what? | Can't you tell anyway?
a : Which way my toes want to point, for a start. | I mean if I had to shut my eyes and guess. Oh, it's harder to explain than to do.

scene mud
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : My chalk ring's turned into a little white river. | I jumped over the mud and landed in the exact same mud.
b : Where's it going? | You didn't jump far enough.
a : Down the gutter to give somebody else a turn. | It went round the corner. Nobody told me mud could do that.

scene mother
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : A whole afternoon with #self.mother# would suit me even with no tart. | I've got something for #self.mother# hidden in my paw.
b : Even with no games? | Is it a surprise?
a : I could make up a game with two stones. So yes. | A polished stone. Pretend I didn't tell you.

scene thunder
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The roof said bang and I ducked before I could stop. | That rumble had two more rumbles hiding behind it.
b : I ducked too. | Are you counting them?
a : We can both say we were looking for #chalk#. | Yes. My toes are braver if they have work.

scene disgruntled
when topic=friends
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm cross because somebody small didn't get a turn. | I shouted so hard about fair turns I didn't hear whose turn it was.
b : Did you give up yours? | And then?
a : I did. Now I'm cross about two things, but one wolf's happy. | I went to the back. I'd do the shouting quieter next time.

scene swimming
when topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I practise kicking while I'm on my belly on the step. | If I can't see my feet in the water, I count my strokes out loud.
b : Does the step take you far? | Why count them?
a : Only in my head. But it never tips me under. | To have something in my ears besides me getting scared.

scene which_news
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : If somebody whispers a thing it sounds twice as true to me. | I'd put a circle round a guess so everybody could see.
b : Or half as true and twice as juicy. | You can't chalk a voice.
a : That's a rotten trick for my ears to play. | Well, I have to ask out loud instead, and then everybody scowls.

scene plum_edges
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The best bit of #slice# is where the purple boils over. | I can share tart exactly by making two cuts.
b : What about the middle? | How's that exact?
a : That's what I trade somebody for the other edge. | You cut, I choose. You watch how careful you get.

scene waiting
when topic=day
does tell.complaint / give.advice / assess
a : Waiting makes my ears hot. I'd rather run there twice. | I've counted every crack on this step already.
b : Set your feet a puzzle. | Try counting what grows in the cracks.
a : Good. I'll stand as still as possible except for my smallest toe. | There's a yellow flower. That one's worth a wait.

story erased [topic=memories]
  : I ruled a whole game out in the dust with the side of my boot.
  : A goat came and stood in the very middle. Couldn't shift it.
  b : Did you play round the goat?
  : Better. We made the goat the winning square. Softest finish to a race I ever had.

rule @mark
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's an empty space inside my chalk! | A place for the littlest boots, right here.

rule @ink
when concept=bark self.job=child
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That letter's the right way up for once! | Ink on my ear. I didn't write with my ear!

dlg @yhub resident.hub : You're close enough now. Want to see?
dlg @yknown resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, come see what I can draw with a broken stub.
dlg @ynight resident.hub [here.time=night] : Speak up. I'm listening for feet on the way home.
dlg @ywary resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Stay beyond the chalk while we talk.
dlg @yjob resident.job [self.job=child] : Letters, sums and trying to rub only the wrong bit off the slate.
dlg @yjob2 resident.job : I've three jobs to finish and I'm keeping count on my toes.
dlg @ybye resident.bye : I'll see if the ring lasts till you come back.

adolescent
line @1 greet : Glad you're here. We can get this going now.
line @1 greet.return : Heard you. Come help me make this fair.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll run the next round myself.
line @1 decline : I've promised my place to somebody who has waited longer.
scene judge
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : They let me judge a race. I set the start and forgot to mark the finish. | I'm teaching little pups to referee.
b : Who won, then? | Do they understand fair play?
a : The first one to notice. I called that good observation. | Down to the last whisker. It's forgiveness they're still working on.

scene badge_colour
when topic=smalltalk
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I'd rather be recognised by my voice than my ribbon. | My badge would be a clean white chalk stroke on a sleeve.
b : Even if it was a fine silk one? | That rubs off.
a : Especially then. Everybody would talk to the ribbon. | Good. I'd have to earn another mark tomorrow.

scene dare
when topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming
does decline / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll swim alongside you but I won't race out of my depth. | Don't count my strokes in front of everybody.
b : Worried I'll win? | Why ever not?
a : Worried we'll both forget which way the bank lies. | I swim straighter when I'm thinking where I'm going.

story boot_swap [topic=memories]
  : I once lent a pup my new boots for a race.
  : They were so big that the pup took two steps to every one the boots took.
  b : Was the pup upset?
  : Delighted. Left one boot in the chalk circle and claimed a place in the next heat.

dlg @adhub resident.hub : Take a moment. I'm old enough to hear you out without calling an assembly.
dlg @adjob resident.job : I keep getting trusted with things I used to have to ask to touch.
dlg @adbye resident.bye : If anyone asks, you had your turn quite properly.
